  "details": "Stations are the only way we can lock players to a position in the world. Locally, stations appear normal, but to remote players, you will not be locked to the station GameObject, but move out of sync with the station. Network IK is syncing positions for the player instead. This \"breaks\" vehicles, avatar stations, and advanced techniques using stations.\n\nSee attached screenshot. Right side is sitting in the station normally. Left side is remote client seeing the person not in the location of the station at all.\n\nTested in the Not Bad Cars world:\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_357d4a0b-6992-4ee0-9a5c-f93c1b2717e7",
